# system_tracer.command output: the .trace bundle is ~38 MB per run and the
# XML/log are regenerable from it. The summary CSV is kept, matching how the
# other verification scripts commit only their *_output/summary files.
# system_tracer.command 的產物：.trace bundle 每次執行約 38 MB，XML 與 log 都可
# 由它重新產生。僅保留 summary CSV，與其他驗證腳本只提交 *_output／summary 的
# 慣例一致。
trace_system/*.trace
trace_system/*.trace.timeout
trace_system/*.thread-state.xml
trace_system/*.record.log
*.xml
powerResults/tmp/
gitOwner.sh
/helper/md-translate/translate_status.txt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
LZFSE_UI.app/
.swift-module-cache/
lzfse-ui/.win-build/
lzfse-ui/release/
helper_windows/.build/
helper_windows/decoded/
helper_windows/release/
helper_windows/lzfse-build-*
helper_windows/claw-code
helper_windows/llama.cpp
helper_windows/bench_logs/rss_tmp*

# run_round.command writes this just before `sudo ./benchmark2.zsh` and removes it
# straight after: sudoers here runs with env_reset, so the settings cannot cross
# the sudo boundary as environment variables. It holds machine-specific paths and
# is regenerated every round, so it must never be committed.
# run_round.command 於 `sudo ./benchmark2.zsh` 之前寫出、之後隨即刪除：本機 sudoers
# 採 env_reset，設定無法以環境變數跨越 sudo 邊界。其中含機器特有路徑且每輪重新產生，
# 故不得入版。
.bench_env
